cff-version: 1.2.0
title: DOE-MCP
message: >-
  If you use this software or its source registry in research, please cite
  it. If you use DATA reached through it, cite the publisher of that data —
  the citation string is in every answer's provenance block, and for some
  sources citation is a condition of use rather than a courtesy.
type: software
authors:
  - name: The DOE-MCP contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/pranava0x0/DOE-MCP
abstract: >-
  MCP servers over public US Department of Energy and national-laboratory
  data, with a provenance envelope on every answer. Covers the ecosystem by
  data domain over a declarative source registry, with an explicit crosswalk
  from all seventeen national laboratories to the platforms that carry their
  data. An independent project, not affiliated with the US Department of
  Energy.
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - open-data
  - energy
  - provenance
  - national-laboratories
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-09-02"
